# Kia Sportage fifth generation five-door, 2022 onwards.
#
# The NQ5 Sportage: the short-wheelbase UK/European body with the boomerang
# rear lamp, the curved display and the larger grille. UK sales from January
# 2022. The long-wheelbase North American body is not represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kia_Sportage
#
# Dimensions 4.515 x 1.865 x 1.650-1.660 m, wheelbase 2.680 m (short-
# wheelbase UK car).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true side elevation of a green five-door;
# the other images show a UK car in front and rear views.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK chart was found. Black, silver, white and green
# are plain names. Weights 15, 13, 12, 10, total 50, provisional.
#
# Speed 205 km/h. Comfort 95/322, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 95. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 2022 intro, retires staggered 2042-2045.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/kia-sportage-5.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/kia-sportage-5.dae. References:
# citycars/references/kia-sportage-5/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: a thin bumper-corner tab is present but does not read at
# 128 px; the arch cladding is a heavy ring. The blacked-out A- and D-pillars
# (floating roof) are not modelled and the greenhouse is shallower than the
# photograph's. At 128 px the shallow glasshouse, boomerang lamps and full-width
# grille panel read as a fifth-generation Sportage.


obj=citycar
name=KiaSportage5(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=15
intro_year=2022
intro_month=1
retire_year=2045
retire_month=6
speed=205
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=95
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=322

